    <statement><p>Let <m>V</m> be a vector space, and <m>T:V \rightarrow V</m> a linear transformation such that 
<m>T(2 \vec{v}_1  - 3 \vec{v}_2)= 3 \vec{v}_1 + 2 \vec{v}_2</m> and <m>T(-3 \vec{v}_1 + 5 \vec{v}_2)= -3 \vec{v}_1  - 5 \vec{v}_2</m>. 
Then</p>
<p><m>T(\vec{v}_1)=</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/> <m>\vec{v}_1+</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0002"/> <m>\vec{v}_2</m>,</p>
<p><m>T(\vec{v}_2)=</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0003"/> <m>\vec{v}_1+</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0004"/> <m>\vec{v}_2</m>,</p>
<p><m>T(-2 \vec{v}_1 + 2 \vec{v}_2)=</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0005"/> <m>\vec{v}_1+</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0006"/> <m>\vec{v}_2</m>.</p>
</statement>
